00:24:57.260 --> 00:24:59.430
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:24:59.430 --> 00:25:02.280
you can pick their pockets,
whatever they have in their

00:25:02.280 --> 00:25:03.110
pocket you can get.

00:25:03.110 --> 00:25:04.870
AUDIENCE: That is still left.

00:25:04.870 --> 00:25:07.521
AUDIENCE: Well you take
it out as you're

00:25:07.521 --> 00:25:08.977
putting the grenade in.

00:25:08.977 --> 00:25:11.033
AUDIENCE: You wouldn't want
their [UNINTELLIGIBLE] to be

00:25:11.033 --> 00:25:11.719
damaged by the grenade.

00:25:11.719 --> 00:25:13.830
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:25:13.830 --> 00:25:14.937
AUDIENCE: Yeah, you're
just putting them

00:25:14.937 --> 00:25:16.260
in at the same time.

00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:18.125
AUDIENCE: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:25:18.125 --> 00:25:20.422
AUDIENCE: And it can
be a little tricky.

00:25:20.422 --> 00:25:21.672
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:25:25.878 --> 00:25:26.870
GUEST SPEAKER: OK.

00:25:26.870 --> 00:25:28.840
Anybody have any representative
examples we

00:25:28.840 --> 00:25:30.286
haven't touched on?

00:25:30.286 --> 00:25:33.258
AUDIENCE: I used to play a lot
of [UNINTELLIGIBLE] online and

00:25:33.258 --> 00:25:34.624
they had a bunch of really
sophisticated rules that

00:25:34.624 --> 00:25:37.040
applied in certain situations.

00:25:37.040 --> 00:25:40.280
So there were a lot of times
in the game where you just

00:25:40.280 --> 00:25:43.172
flat out lie to people and have
them go into situations

00:25:43.172 --> 00:25:45.000
that were unsafe for them.

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:47.950
For example, if people were in
your house-- in an urban

00:25:47.950 --> 00:25:49.750
[UNINTELLIGIBLE] game if people
are inside your house

00:25:49.750 --> 00:25:53.390
they are automatically flagged
as attackable by you because

00:25:53.390 --> 00:25:56.155
they're in your house and you
might not have let them in.

00:25:56.155 --> 00:25:57.990
And they can run outside their
house and they'll be

00:25:57.990 --> 00:25:58.730
unattackable by you.

00:25:58.730 --> 00:26:01.930
But you can also put a trash
barrel in front of your door,

00:26:01.930 --> 00:26:04.480
which only you can destroy and
nobody else can destroy, and

00:26:04.480 --> 00:26:05.910
they can't run through that.

00:26:05.910 --> 00:26:08.570
So you would invite them in
to trade them something or

00:26:08.570 --> 00:26:09.395
enjoying your meal.

00:26:09.395 --> 00:26:11.830
And they're in your house, then
you put a trash barrel

00:26:11.830 --> 00:26:16.000
there so they can never leave
and just kill them.

00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:16.740
GUEST SPEAKER: Or just leave
them there, right?

00:26:16.740 --> 00:26:17.710
AUDIENCE: Or just leave them.

00:26:17.710 --> 00:26:19.640
There are tons and
tons of rules.

00:26:19.640 --> 00:26:21.490
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

00:26:21.490 --> 00:26:23.645
It's really bad, It's
really bad.

00:26:23.645 --> 00:26:27.889
I was part of the Guild that
did this to me and then I

00:26:27.889 --> 00:26:28.887
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:26:28.887 --> 00:26:30.883
I was like, that
is pretty sick.

00:26:30.883 --> 00:26:33.378
There are a bunch of way to
steal tons and tons of money

00:26:33.378 --> 00:26:35.873
from people and they didn't
realize that you did.

00:26:35.873 --> 00:26:37.370
GUEST SPEAKER: Did you get
that [UNINTELLIGIBLE]?

00:26:37.370 --> 00:26:38.368
AUDIENCE: Yeah.

00:26:38.368 --> 00:26:38.867
Yes.

00:26:38.867 --> 00:26:43.460
But I feel like just blatantly
lying to people as a tactic

00:26:43.460 --> 00:26:45.310
instead of just being
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:26:48.150 --> 00:26:51.713
AUDIENCE: The question about
real world money for in game

00:26:51.713 --> 00:26:56.555
items especially for competitive
games whether or

00:26:56.555 --> 00:26:58.501
not it's allowed by the GMs.

00:27:02.140 --> 00:27:03.556
Those are two different
questions.

00:27:03.556 --> 00:27:05.640
One is the ethical question from
the player's standpoint.

00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:09.119
And the other is what does it
mean in terms of the player

00:27:09.119 --> 00:27:12.430
character relation
in the game.

00:27:12.430 --> 00:27:16.230
AUDIENCE: I was going to say
one thing that comes up

00:27:16.230 --> 00:27:19.900
especially in board games that
have a lot of positive

00:27:19.900 --> 00:27:23.030
feedback, it's called
king making.

00:27:23.030 --> 00:27:24.315
Good examples are like
in Monopoly,

00:27:24.315 --> 00:27:25.530
or Settlers or Munchkin.

00:27:25.530 --> 00:27:29.375
And how it works, let's say you
and Owen and I are playing

00:27:29.375 --> 00:27:33.000
Settlers and typically what
will happen is say Owen is

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:35.750
winning but I'm typically really
far behind, or someone

00:27:35.750 --> 00:27:38.250
is going to be in a position
where they have

00:27:38.250 --> 00:27:39.540
no chance of winning.

00:27:39.540 --> 00:27:42.123
So if I decide he's winning and
you're close second and

00:27:42.123 --> 00:27:45.271
I'm distant third, what people
do is say, hey Mia, I will

00:27:45.271 --> 00:27:47.640
give you everything for your one
little card and then you

00:27:47.640 --> 00:27:50.390
can win because I'm
mad at Owen.

00:27:50.390 --> 00:27:52.844
And then it comes up, like you
said, in Monopoly there's this

00:27:52.844 --> 00:27:55.356
question of is that a really
jerky thing to do?

00:27:55.356 --> 00:27:56.832
The rules don't disallow it.

00:27:56.832 --> 00:27:59.292
It's an ongoing debate.

00:27:59.292 --> 00:28:01.752
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:28:01.752 --> 00:28:03.720
GUEST SPEAKER: Don't do that.

00:28:03.720 --> 00:28:06.672
AUDIENCE: Similarly in Monopoly,
the rules don't

00:28:06.672 --> 00:28:08.640
specifically allow If I have
two [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:28:08.640 --> 00:28:12.820
we'll exchange that and promise
each other immunity on

00:28:12.820 --> 00:28:14.940
our properties or something
that you're not allowed to

00:28:14.940 --> 00:28:15.730
actually promise each other.

00:28:15.730 --> 00:28:17.760
Or if [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:20.632
will always do it to you and
will promise me half the

00:28:20.632 --> 00:28:23.246
profits or something like that
where clearly the third person

00:28:23.246 --> 00:28:26.418
is now shut out of the game
and can't win because

00:28:26.418 --> 00:28:27.412
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:28:27.412 --> 00:28:31.388
advantage even though we're
[UNINTELLIGIBLE] with things

00:28:31.388 --> 00:28:33.376
that aren't explicitly
allowed in the rules.

00:28:33.376 --> 00:28:37.120
GUEST SPEAKER: How many of you
have played Dragon Age?

00:28:37.120 --> 00:28:39.595
AUDIENCE: I've seen it played.

00:28:39.595 --> 00:28:40.585
