00:30:20.920 --> 00:30:24.810
And they're pretty good,
and they're bad.

00:30:24.810 --> 00:30:27.025
GUEST SPEAKER: I just chose
poorly, apparently, my

00:30:27.025 --> 00:30:28.100
companions [INAUDIBLE]

00:30:28.100 --> 00:30:32.040
moralistic ones like
kill a kid.

00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:33.780
OK.

00:30:33.780 --> 00:30:35.350
In the reading you did
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:30:35.350 --> 00:30:39.600
talks about different choices
and the way that game

00:30:39.600 --> 00:30:41.550
designers are putting
games together.

00:30:41.550 --> 00:30:44.320
And he talks about two different
categories, the open

00:30:44.320 --> 00:30:46.035
and the closed ethical
systems.

00:30:48.780 --> 00:30:53.100
The open was more letting
players determine for

00:30:53.100 --> 00:30:55.710
themselves [UNINTELLIGIBLE] they
want to take and kind of

00:30:55.710 --> 00:30:58.730
seeing how that goes through,
whereas the closed is the

00:30:58.730 --> 00:31:03.100
system that forces a
particular way of

00:31:03.100 --> 00:31:05.080
playing upon you.

00:31:05.080 --> 00:31:08.440
And so, just kind of going
through these here, where do

00:31:08.440 --> 00:31:12.570
you see them falling in terms
of closed and open?

00:31:12.570 --> 00:31:14.800
AUDIENCE: Wait.

00:31:14.800 --> 00:31:17.134
You confused me with those
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:31:17.134 --> 00:31:19.614
You said open means that you
have the decision on how to

00:31:19.614 --> 00:31:23.270
value actions or
on what to do?

00:31:23.270 --> 00:31:25.850
GUEST SPEAKER: Well he says, for
example, in The Sims with

00:31:25.850 --> 00:31:29.840
drowning, he mentions The Sims
is an open game where you can

00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:36.990
do what you want and think
about what happens.

00:31:36.990 --> 00:31:39.200
AUDIENCE: A definitely closed
example, it's not up there,

00:31:39.200 --> 00:31:40.180
but I'll give you a closed
example up there

00:31:40.180 --> 00:31:42.050
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:31:42.050 --> 00:31:46.220
In the first Modern Warfare
game they have a flashback

00:31:46.220 --> 00:31:50.230
sequence where you have to snipe
the featured bad guy,

00:31:50.230 --> 00:31:51.640
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:31:51.640 --> 00:31:57.110
And even though in the game
story he survives your attempt

00:31:57.110 --> 00:32:00.780
to kill him, if you don't
actually hit him with the

00:32:00.780 --> 00:32:04.390
bullet the game won't
let you progress.

00:32:04.390 --> 00:32:08.240
So you have to go and basically
snipe this dude no

00:32:08.240 --> 00:32:10.080
matter what, the game
won't let you do it.

00:32:10.080 --> 00:32:10.530
And that's just part
of the story,

00:32:10.530 --> 00:32:11.870
that's just how it works.

00:32:11.870 --> 00:32:15.530
And it's dubiously moral that
you should be meddling with

00:32:15.530 --> 00:32:16.980
such affairs but you know.

00:32:16.980 --> 00:32:19.590
And it actually comes back to
bite you later in the game

00:32:19.590 --> 00:32:23.250
because you're at the place
where it's causing problems

00:32:23.250 --> 00:32:25.134
for you the fact that you
tried snipe this guy.

00:32:25.134 --> 00:32:26.660
And they had you play
the flashback but

00:32:26.660 --> 00:32:28.820
you have to do it.

00:32:28.820 --> 00:32:32.256
And it's all directed
[UNINTELLIGIBLE].

00:32:32.256 --> 00:32:34.720
AUDIENCE: Isn't like the Cube
