00:40:25.280 --> 00:40:28.260
Kaldor dueled me, left my
party, and then tried to

00:40:28.260 --> 00:40:30.710
attack me because
I was too evil.

00:40:30.710 --> 00:40:31.690
AUDIENCE: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:40:31.690 --> 00:40:32.460
AUDIENCE: [UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:40:32.460 --> 00:40:32.990
I stood out.

00:40:32.990 --> 00:40:35.440
Like very, very specific actions
that will affect your

00:40:35.440 --> 00:40:37.795
alignment, and there aren't
very many of those.

00:40:37.795 --> 00:40:41.310
In addition you have these cut
scene decisions, which are

00:40:41.310 --> 00:40:43.326
also very black or white,
good or evil.

00:40:43.326 --> 00:40:45.522
But I would say there's a lot of
decisions in the game that

00:40:45.522 --> 00:40:49.470
don't [UNINTELLIGIBLE], that
have both that ethical choice

00:40:49.470 --> 00:40:54.980
but not nearly as much of
a mechanical impact.

00:40:54.980 --> 00:40:57.010
GUEST SPEAKER: One of the things
he also mentions in

00:40:57.010 --> 00:41:00.508
relation to the open system,
going back to The Sims, is

00:41:00.508 --> 00:41:05.470
that you can do what you want
and the game doesn't

00:41:05.470 --> 00:41:08.040
necessarily punish you.

00:41:08.040 --> 00:41:11.480
You can murder and you can drown
your Sims, and the rest

00:41:11.480 --> 00:41:15.290
of the Sims in the house don't
move away in fear or

00:41:15.290 --> 00:41:18.010
disapprove of your action.

00:41:18.010 --> 00:41:20.270
It's just up to you whether
you want to feel

00:41:20.270 --> 00:41:21.840
bad about it or not.

00:41:21.840 --> 00:41:27.990
Or the game has no larger
response other than let a Sim

00:41:27.990 --> 00:41:31.745
die once the site lit
a Sim on fire.

00:41:31.745 --> 00:41:36.200
And I wish they rolled for his
life and got a zombie back.

00:41:36.200 --> 00:41:39.830
It turns out the only way
zombies happen in the game is

00:41:39.830 --> 00:41:40.655
